---
import { mastheadStamp } from "../dossiers/headline.js";
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import EveryCut from './EveryCut.astro';
import GuideData from './GuideData.astro';
import {monthYearStamp} from '../dossiers/display.js';
import {bySlug,kicker} from '../dossiers/registry.js';
import {pensionsModel} from '../dossiers/pensions.model.js';
import {pensionFormat} from '../dossiers/pensions.format.js';
import {governedPensionPayload,governedPensionPayloadText} from '../dossiers/pensions.payload.js';
interface Props { model?: any; entry?: any }
const D=Astro.props.entry??bySlug.pensions,model=Astro.props.model??pensionsModel();
if(!D||D.sourceQualityMode!=='required')throw Error('Governed pension guide registry is required');
const inputs=model.manifest.bundles.map(b=>b.slug).join(', '),h=model.headline;
const groups=[...new Set(model.plates.map(p=>p.sourceId))].map(id=>({id,plates:model.plates.filter(p=>p.sourceId===id)}));
const stockIds=new Set(['A1','A2','A3','M2','M3']);
const sections=[{title:'The account stocks and the money held',groups:groups.filter(g=>stockIds.has(g.id))},{title:'Registrations, administrative cases and expected timing',groups:groups.filter(g=>!stockIds.has(g.id))}];
const payload=governedPensionPayload(model.plates),sourceURL='https://www.pfrda.org.in/en/research-publications/statistics/statistical-data';
---
<Base title="Pensions and retirement saving · India Atlas" description={D.description} nav="guides" dateStamp={mastheadStamp(D)} crumbLeft='<a href="/guides/">Guides</a> / Households / <b>Pensions</b>' crumbRight={`${D.statusNote}, <b>${D.version}</b>`} canonical="https://atlas.thisindianlife.today/guides/pensions/" ogImage="/og/pensions.png">
<div class="page pensions-guide">
 <div class="titleblock break" data-inputs={h.bundle} data-prose="evergreen and source-bound facts">
  <div class="kicker">{kicker(D)}</div><div class="hero-grid"><h1 set:html={D.headline}/><p class="lede">An account records participation in a scheme. Contributions add money; investments hold it; an annuity can pay income later. These administrative records describe separate stages of retirement saving under the National Pension System and Atal Pension Yojana.</p></div>
  <div class="meta"><span>Source period <b>{h.lastSourcePeriod}</b></span><span>Measure <b>Published subscriber stock</b></span><span>Data revision date <b>Not published</b></span></div>
  <div class="numbers"><div class="num"><div class="l">Atal Pension Yojana subscribers</div><div class="v acc" id="n-pensions-apy" data-source-bundle={h.bundle} data-source-key={h.key}>{pensionFormat(h.lastSourceValue,h.unit)}</div><div class="d">Source month-end count; account activity and unique-person coverage are not established</div></div></div>
 </div>
 <section data-inputs={h.bundle} data-prose="evergreen"><div class="sec-head"><h2>Saving for expenses after work</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="reading-cols"><div class="reading-col"><p>A household needs to know whether saving can continue through interruptions in income and whether accumulated money will meet later expenses. An account count answers neither question. It does not show the frequency of contributions or the adequacy of retirement income.</p></div><div class="reading-col"><p>An investment balance can change with prices, transfers and money entering or leaving. Reading it as a contribution flow would combine different measures. Each source series below keeps its published unit, period and definition.</p></div></div></section>
 <section data-inputs={inputs} data-prose="methodology"><div class="sec-head"><h2>How to read these records</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="wm-grid"><div><p><b>Start with what is counted.</b> Subscriber stocks, registrations and annuity cases are different administrative measures. Their source definitions remain with their tables. They do not establish a count of unique people, active accounts or all eligible workers.</p><p><b>Read each history separately.</b> Each chart contains one exact source record. Sector and scheme columns can overlap. A total and its components are not added, and these charts do not certify comparisons between populations.</p><p><b>Keep source endpoints visible.</b> Each chart ends at its own last published value. Earlier pension-fund histories retain their source labels and last endpoint. They are not described as current operations or ranked by performance.</p><p><b>Expected schedules remain expected.</b> The retirement criteria, source fiscal years and unknown forecast snapshot stay visible. Expected entries are not realised exits or future pension payments.</p><p><b>Keep unresolved meanings separate.</b> Unreviewed values and units remain available in labelled archival JSON and original workbooks. Pending records have no numeric chart or interpreted export. Held territorial or unit/basis records remain in the original-workbook inventory.</p><p><b>Retain missing observations.</b> A source dash or blank stays missing. No missing figure becomes zero and no date, boundary or forecast snapshot is supplied from a different edition.</p></div><div class="wm-rail"><aside class="margin-note"><span class="mk">Accounts and people</span>These records do not supply a matching population denominator for a retirement-coverage rate.</aside><aside class="margin-note"><span class="mk">Source version</span>Workbook hashes identify the retained source bodies. Capture dates and report editions do not establish data revision dates.</aside></div></div></section>
 <section id="current-reading" data-inputs={inputs} data-prose="source-bound facts"><div class="sec-head"><h2>The reviewed records and the remaining source coverage</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="reading-cols"><div class="reading-col"><p>The headline uses APY's published stock at <b>{h.lastSourcePeriod}</b>. The guide draws <b>{model.coverage.reviewedObservedRecords}</b> reviewed observed records and <b>{model.coverage.reviewedExpectedRecords}</b> separately labelled expected records. Each record has its own source period and endpoint.</p><p>No household-income, regular-contribution or pension-adequacy conclusion is calculated from these counts.</p></div><div class="reading-col"><p>The register retains <b>{model.coverage.pendingRecords}</b> pending records with their source identities and review status. Another <b>{model.coverage.sourceOnlyRecords}</b> records remain source-only while territorial scope, units or contribution basis are unresolved. The complete source inventory links every retained original workbook.</p><p>Archival access preserves the data for inspection. It does not validate an unresolved measure or turn an expected count into an observed result.</p></div></div></section>
 {sections.map(section=><section data-inputs={inputs} data-prose="source definitions and bound facts"><div class="sec-head"><h2>{section.title}</h2><span class="line"></span></div>{section.groups.map(g=>{
  const sample=g.plates[0],expected=sample.observationKind==='expected-schedule';
  return <div class="pension-source-group" id={'source-'+g.id}><h3>{sample.meta.product}</h3>{[...new Set(g.plates.map(p=>p.definition))].map(def=><p>{def}</p>)}{[...new Set(g.plates.map(p=>p.referenceBasis))].map(ref=><p class="pension-basis">{ref}</p>)}{expected&&<div class="pension-expected-note"><p><b>Expected schedule. Forecast snapshot: unknown.</b> {sample.meta.forecastWindowNote}</p><p class="source-note">{sample.meta.note}</p></div>}{!expected&&sample.sourceNote&&<details><summary>Published source note</summary><p class="source-note">{sample.sourceNote}</p></details>}{g.plates.map(p=><figure id={'cb-'+p.id} class="break" data-inputs={p.bundle} data-series-key={p.lines[0].key} data-observation-kind={p.sourceQuality.observationKind}><div class="plate-head"><div class="t"><h3>{p.title}</h3><div class="sub">{p.observationKind==='expected-schedule'?'Expected schedule. Forecast snapshot: unknown.':'Exact published source history.'} Last source entry: {p.period}. {p.unit==='inr_crore'?'Rupees, crore.':'Published count.'}</div></div><div class="plate-val"><div class="v" id={'pv-'+p.id}>{pensionFormat(p.rows[0].value,p.unit)}</div><div class="c">{p.observationKind==='expected-schedule'?'Expected source entry':'Last published source entry'}</div></div></div><div class="frame"><div class="plotzone" id={'plot-'+p.id}></div><div class="plotfoot"><span class="src">Source: PFRDA, {p.sourceId}. <a href={p.sourceUrl}>Publisher workbook</a>. <a href={'#source-'+p.sourceId}>Definition and source basis</a>.</span><div class="dl"><button data-dl="svg">SVG</button><button data-dl="png">PNG</button><button data-dl="csv">CSV</button></div></div></div>{p.sourceCategoryRole==='overlapping-source-total'&&<p class="pension-total-note">This is a published aggregate. Do not add it to its components.</p>}</figure>)}</div>;
 })}</section>)}
 <section data-inputs={inputs} data-prose="evergreen and source provenance"><div class="sec-head"><h2>Misreadings and the path back to the source</h2><span class="line"></span></div><p><b>“An account means regular saving.”</b> The reviewed account stocks do not establish regular contribution activity.</p><p><b>“The largest balance means the best performance.”</b> Source AUM histories do not isolate returns or create a comparable performance ranking.</p><p><b>“Expected exits are completed exits.”</b> The source schedule applies administrative retirement criteria. It does not report realised events or amounts paid.</p><p><b>“These are all India's retirement arrangements.”</b> The source concerns the schemes and records published by PFRDA. A whole-population coverage rate is not calculated.</p><p>Each plotted number is tied to its source bundle, record, workbook hash and source cell. <a href={sourceURL}>Publisher statistical tables</a>. The source inventory below preserves the original workbooks and separates reviewed, pending and held records. Data revision dates remain unpublished where the workbook does not attest them.</p><p id="prov-vintage">Source revision date: not published.</p></section>
 <EveryCut slug="pensions"/><GuideData slug="pensions"/>
</div>
<script is:inline type="application/json" id="pensions-data" set:html={governedPensionPayloadText(payload)}/>
<script>import '../dossiers/pensions.client.js';import '../dossiers/guide.client.js';</script>
</Base>
<style is:global>
 .pensions-guide .plotzone>svg[data-compact="pensions"]{min-width:0;max-width:100%;height:auto}
 .pension-source-group{margin-top:36px}.pension-source-group>h3{margin-bottom:12px}
 .pension-basis,.pension-total-note{color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem}
 .pension-expected-note{border-left:2px solid var(--rule);padding-left:18px;margin:18px 0}
 .source-note{white-space:pre-line;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
 .pensions-guide .plate-val .v{font-size:clamp(1.2rem,2.7vw,1.8rem)}
</style>
